#
# Competency question: "Which standpoint is each recommendation held from, and
# over which interval?"
#
# This is the question the operator review projection cannot answer, and saying
# so is the slice's own disclosed loss: collapsing coexisting standpoint-indexed
# classifications into one readable surface is a real loss, which is why the
# review ships a projection receipt rather than presenting the collapse as the
# record. This query is the uncollapsed form — the rows the receipt is admitting
# it dropped.
#
# The standpoint index and the time scope are REUSED, never re-minted: the
# vantage a comparison is framed from is the core gmeow:Standpoint, and the
# interval it is scoped to is the core gmeow:TimeScopedRelation, reached exactly
# as every other time-scoped claim in the ontology reaches one.
#
# Over the contextual-recommendation scene this returns three rows sharing ONE
# interval — three readings of the same decision moment from three standpoints,
# not one decision revisited later under new information. That distinction is
# what makes their disagreement a genuine coexistence rather than a change of
# mind, and it is only visible because the time scope is recorded.

PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>

SELECT ?context ?standpoint ?interval WHERE {
    ?context a gmeow:ComparisonContext ;
             gmeow:contextStandpoint ?standpoint ;
             gmeow:contextTime ?scope .
    ?standpoint a gmeow:Standpoint .
    ?scope a gmeow:TimeScopedRelation ;
           gmeow:duringInterval ?interval .
}
ORDER BY ?context ?standpoint
